        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Change Order Audit Violations Report"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1769232242891"
          },
          "code": "CHANGE_ORDER_AUDIT_VIOLATIONS_REPORT",
          "id": "1766125339886",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1766125339887_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "* Mark all ERROR values as FAIL and display them in red bold text.\n* Always print the \"Audit Violations Summary for Change Order\" section at the top\n  of the report only once; do not repeat it at the end.\n* Print all table column headers in black bold text, left aligned.\n\n1. Extract data from {{$context.$nodes.FORMAT_AUDIT_MESSAGE.$output.FormatedAuditViolations}}\n   and display it under the heading \"Change Order Rule Audit Violations Summary\" as an HTML\n   table sorted by Serial No.\n   - Use {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.ChangeNotice}} as the Object if empty.\n   - If any row other than the first has Severity FAIL, override it to WARNING.\n   - If the data is empty, add a single row with the text \"No Violations\" and end the table.\n\n2. Extract data from {{$context.$nodes.GENERATE_CUSTOM_RULE_BASED_AUDIT_VIOLATIONS.$output.GenerateCustomRuleBasedAuditViolationsOutput}}\n   and display it under the heading \"Custom Validation Rules Audit Violations\" as an HTML\n   table with columns:\n   1. Objects <- Object Value\n   2. Attributes Value\n   3. Change Order Type from Rule\n   4. Conditions from Rule\n   5. Validation Status\n   - Reorder rows so that rows with Validation Status = FAIL appear first, followed by WARNING, then PASS.\n   - Use Times font for table rows.\n   - Do not print \"TOTAL VIOLATIONS\" at the end of this table.\n   - If the data is empty, add a single row with the text \"No Violations\" and end the table.\n3. Add a Serial number to the table \"Custom Validation Rules Audit Violations\" as SR#\n4. Audit Violations Summary:\n   - Combine data from both tables to produce an Executive Summary including totals of:\n     1. FAIL (sum of FAIL counts from both tables)\n     2. WARNINGS (sum of WARNINGS counts from both tables)\n     3. VIOLATIONS (sum of VIOLATIONS counts from both tables)\n     4. PASS (sum of PASS counts from both tables)\n     5. PASS percentage\n     6. Overall Validation Status: PASS or FAIL based on results\n     7. Disposition and Recommended Actions\n     8. \"Change Order Status: \" + {{$context.$variables.ChangeOrderStatus}} in bold blue\n     9. \"Change Order Type: \" + {{$context.$variables.ChangeOrderType}} in bold blue\n   - Display FAIL values in red bold, WARNINGS in orange bold, PASS and PASS % in green\n     bold, and TOTAL VIOLATIONS in bold, separated by \"|\".\n   - Summarize violations and disposition action items based on reported violations.\n   - Include a message instructing the user to rerun the report after fixing violations.\n   - Print this Executive Summary under the heading \"Audit Violations Summary for Change Order \"\n     + {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.ChangeNotice}} before the first table.\n\n5. Extract the deep link from {{$context.$nodes.GENERATE_CHANGE_ORDER_DEEP_LINK.$output.deeplink}}\n   and print it as:\n   <span>To open Change Order click here: <a href='{deep link}' target='_blank'>\n   {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.ChangeNotice}}</a></span>\n   below the \"Change Order Type:\" line.\n   - Do not print the label \"Deep Link\".\n\n6. Mandatory formatting and output rules:\n   - Print the full report in landscape format.\n   - Do not use background CSS or color table cells; only text color is allowed.\n   - Do not include any JSON conversion instructions.\n   - Do not print any additional details after the two tables.\n   - Ensure the tally of FAIL and WARNING counts from both tables matches the summary.\n   - Print the Executive Summary first, then \"Change Order Rule Audit Violations Summary\",\n     then \"Custom Validation Rules Audit Violations\".\n   - Do not print the Executive Summary at the bottom.\n   - Print \"Change Order Status\" and \"Change Order Type\" below Overall Validation Status,\n     separated by \"|\".\n\nFollow these instructions precisely to produce a clear, well-formatted HTML report\nwith correct sorting, coloring, and summary data as specified."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"ChangeOrderAuditViolationsReportOutput\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
