        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Generate Custom Rule Based Audit Violations"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1766125339886"
          },
          "code": "GENERATE_CUSTOM_RULE_BASED_AUDIT_VIOLATIONS",
          "id": "1767735097814",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1767735097815_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "### IMPORTANT INSTRUCTION for Rule Evaluation:\n\n1. Extract data from {{$context.$nodes.UPLOAD_CUSTOM_CHANGE_ORDER_AUDIT_RULES.$output.value}} as a table.\n   For each row, perform the following steps:\n\n2. Rules for attribute extraction:\n  2.1 If AttributeGroup = Change Standard Attributes, apply rules to attributes from {{$context.$nodes.GET_CHANGE_ORDER_DETAILS.$output}}.\n  2.2 If AttributeGroup = Change DFF Attributes, apply rules to attributes from {{$context.$nodes.GET_CHANGE_ORDER_FLEX_FIELDS.$output}}.\n  2.3 If AttributeGroup = Change EFF Attributes, apply rules to attributes from {{$context.$nodes.GET_CHANGE_ORDER_FLEX_FIELDS.$output}}.\n  2.4 If AttributeGroup = Change Order Affected Object, apply rules to attributes from {{$context.$nodes.GET_AFFECTED_ITEM_ID_FOR_CHANGE_ORDER.$output}}.\n  2.5 If AttributeGroup = Change Line Attributes, apply rules to attributes from both {{$context.$nodes.GET_CHANGE_ORDER_LINE_ATTRIBUTES.$output}} and {{$context.$nodes.AFFECTED_ITEMS_PENDING_CHANGE_ORDERS.$output}}.\n  2.6 If AttributeGroup = Change Line DFF, apply rules to attributes from {{$context.$nodes.GET_CHANGE_ORDER_LINE_DESCRIPTIVE_FLEXFIELDS.$output}}.\n\n3. Task Instructions:\n  - For each Change Order Type and Attribute Group, read the list of attributes specified in the Attributes column for the given condition.\n  - Extract current attribute values only for those attributes.\n  - Do not split attributes from the same Attribute Set (from Rule) into multiple rows; evaluate and report them as a single row.\n  - Evaluate one condition at a time against the extracted attribute value(s).\n  - If NewLifecyclePhaseValue is null, set it to OldLifecyclePhaseValue.\n  - Evaluate the condition only when OldLifecyclePhaseValue and NewLifecyclePhaseValue differ.\n  - For each Object Value, attribute set, condition, and Change Order Type, determine the result as PASS, WARNING, or FAILURE based solely on whether the condition is satisfied.\n  - Do not combine or chain conditions during evaluation.\n  - Report each evaluated condition as a separate row.\n\n4. Output Requirements:\n  - Output results in a table titled **Custom Rules Audit Violations** as the table header.\n  - Print one audit violation row per rule violation.\n  - Set the Disposition column value based on PASS/FAIL/WARNING according to the rule outcome.\n\n5. Table Columns:\n  1. Objects (Attribute Group)\n  2. Object Value: If Objects = Change Notice, set to {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.ChangeNotice}}; if Objects = Change Line, set to ItemNumber.\n  3. Attribute From Rule: Comma-separated attribute name and value pairs.\n  4. Change Order Type from Rule.\n  5. Conditions from Rule.\n  6. Validation Status.\n  7. Violation.\n\n6. Rules for Printing:\n  - Entity Printing:\n    - Use entity=ChangeNotice if Attribute Group is Change Standard Attributes, Change DFF Attributes, Change EFF Attributes, or Change Order Affected Object.\n    - Use entity=Change Line if Attribute Group is Change Line Attributes.\n  - Reorder table rows so that:\n    1. All rows with Disposition = FAIL appear first.\n    2. Followed by rows with Disposition = WARNING.\n    3. Followed by rows with Disposition = PASS.\n  - Color code Validation Status column:\n    - FAIL in bold red.\n    - WARNING in bold orange.\n    - PASS in bold green.\n    - TOTAL VIOLATIONS in bold.\n  - Use Times font for table rows.\n  - Do NOT print ChangeLineId.\n  - Do NOT wrap column headings.\n  - Use color coding only for the Validation Status column.\n\nDo NOT include any JSON conversion details in the output.\n"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"GenerateCustomRuleBasedAuditViolationsOutput\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Format Audit Message"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1766125339886"
          },
          "code": "FORMAT_AUDIT_MESSAGE",
          "id": "1774932342652",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1774932342653_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Extract data from {{$context.$nodes.EXTRACT_AUDIT_VIOLATIONS.$output.result}}. Include the\nfollowing columns: Status Name, Sequence Number, Status Code, Criteria Type (Entry / Exit /\nValidation), Category, Messages (bulleted list within the cell), Severity (color-coded using\n<span>), and Data Formatting Rules. Instructions:\n1. Sort rows by Sequence Number in ascending order.\n2. Group violations into one row as a bulleted list for the same Status and same object. If there are no\nviolations for a group, set Severity to PASS.\n3. Create a table titled \"REST Based Audit Violations\" with these columns:\n   - Status: use Status Name.\n   - Objects: use Category; if null or \"General Information\", replace with {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.ChangeNotice}}.\n   - Violation: Messages as a bulleted list within the cell.\n   - Severity.\n4. Remove row from table if it has no violations.\n5. For Objects null, replace with {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.ChangeNotice}}.\n6. For all rows except the first, set Severity to WARNING. This rule must be applied without exception. If any row other than the first has Severity other than WARNING, override it to WARNING.\n7. For repeated violations, list only the one with the smallest Sequence Number.\n8. Add a serial number column to the \"REST Based Audit Violations\" table as SR#.\n9. Above the table, print counts in this format: \"Fail Count: \" + Fail Count + \" Warning Count: \"\n   + Warning Count + \" Total Count: \" + Total Count.\nRecommended Action Items: Summarize under the heading \"Recommended Action\" before the\n\"REST Based Audit Violations\" table.\nReport formatting rules for the HTML table:\n- Display Fail severity in red and Warning in orange.\n- Display Fail Count in red, Warning Count in orange, and Total Count in blue.\n- Use Times font throughout.\n- Do NOT use any external style sheets.\nEnsure all instructions are followed precisely and output is clean, well-structured HTML.\n"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"FormatedAuditViolations\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
